      legacy:'The word "dunce" derives (unfairly) from "Duns-man" — followers of Scotus mocked by Renaissance humanists who thought Scholastic subtlety was pointless. His concept of haecceity influenced Peirce, and his univocity of being influenced Deleuze. His voluntarism anticipates later debates about divine command theory in ethics.',
